<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74451" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀπῐκοί</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Opici</i> or <i>Osci
			(Opsci,</i> Fest.<i><span class="en">
				p.218
			</span></i> L.), an ancient people of Southern Italy, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1329b19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.4.3
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄπικες</span></b> , v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.2
			</span></i> ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀπικία</span></b> , ἡ, <i>their country,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i> : hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀπικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<i>barbarous,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				5.131
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Juv.
				3.207
			</span></i> : hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπικίζω</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρβαρίζω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Mens.</u>
				1.13
			</span></i>, as 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀππικίζω</span>
			 ; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφφικίζω</span> ibid. :
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀππικιστής</span></b> ,
				<i>opicus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i></div>
